    "key-numeral-cipher": {
      "normalized_latin": "Iaaihid ifeib, ieifeigeicchkib. cakeihid. i&kahk. gidibid. eigih. ieeigigh ibkig. &kif. iaaihifid, ibeicdaka eih. icei&kaib.",
      "reason": "The type on C ii verso gives i&kahk, &kif and icei&kaib. C ii recto assigns the cipher group i& to q and the single ampersand to f. The open-foot h can be distinguished from the closed b in the same lines. The inter-group punctuation is regularized and the line breaks are represented by spaces. The unusual i&kahk is transcribed as printed. The BSB copy agrees with HAB Fb 128 on these letters. The dot or small stroke following ibeicdaka is treated as a separator.",
